[x] add a new task
[x] change the status of a task
[x] move tasks between files
[x] change the due date of a task
[x] change the description of a task ('xit edit <task_id> <new_description>')
[x] change the priority of a task ('xit prio <task_id> <new_priority>')
[x] add or remove tags from/to a task ('xit tag <task_id> <tag>' and 'xit untag <task_id> <tag>' commands)
[x] remove tasks permanently
[x] list tasks + filter according to attributes
[ ] log all xit commands you used ('xit log' to view) log file is stored in ~/.xit/log.txt
[ ] undo the last X xit commands executed ('xit undo <number>'), needs to be confirmed by the user
[ ] create a configuration file to set default things (e.g. color scheme, default keywords -> #created=2025-10-20)
    'xit config' to create/edit -> opens in default text editor e.g. vim
[x] xit stats command to show statistics about tasks
[x] support for multiple task files (e.g., work.xit, personal.xit)
[x] support for recurring tasks ('xit recur <task_id> -i <interval> -e <end_date> -f <file> -n <number_of_occurrences>')
[x] support for batch operations on multiple tasks at once (e.g., 'xit mark 1 2 3 --done' to mark tasks 1, 2, and 3 as done)
[ ] find tasks by keyword in description ('xit find <keyword>')
[ ] find out the history of a task (when it was created, modified, marked done, etc.) ('xit history <task_id>')
[x] sort tasks by different attributes (due date, priority) ('xit show -f <file> --sort <attribute> --order <asc/desc>')
[x] create test for xit show -f tests/files/examples2.xit --sort due_date
